{{also|Heathen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Germanic: from {{etyl|ang}} ''[[hæþen|hǣþen]]'', akin to ''[[heath]]'' on the moor, the poor, 'wild' countryside; cognate with Dutch ''[[heiden]]'', German ''[[Heide]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|iːðən}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# not adhering to an [[Abrahamic]] [[religion]]; [[pagan]].
# {{by extension}} uncultured; uncivilized; savage, [[philistine]].
# {{alternative capitalization of|Heathen|nodot=1}} {{qualifier|pertaining or adhering to the Germanic [[neo-pagan]] faith [[Heathenry]]}}.

